From 28b8496ba552aafd3ed50b02fe7ca2478f5f5c0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Ruhier <aruhier@mailbox.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:34:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x: document GPIO
 71

The purpose of the GPIO 71 pin in the x1e80100 Yoga Slim 7x was unknown.

By decoding the Windows DSDT, I saw that it describes it as the
card-detect GPIO of the SD card controller (SDC2 _CRS: GpioInt (Edge,
ActiveBoth, SharedAndWake, PullUp) and GpioIo (PullUp) on pin 71).

The Slim 7x has no SD card reader, which could explain why the pin is
bridged with pin 92.

Rename the pin state from lid-pull-n-pins to sd-cd-n-pins accordingly.

Signed-off-by: Anthony Ruhier <aruhier@mailbox.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
index 558e3fe1f94e..d204be5e8a62 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
@@ -1555,9 +1555,12 @@
 		 * events). By default, pin 71 is set as output-high, which blocks any
 		 * event on pin 92. Output-disable on pin 71 is necessary to get events on
 		 * pin 92.
-		 * The purpose of pin 71 is not yet known; lid-pull is a supposition.
+		 * In the ACPI tables, pin 71 is the card-detect GPIO of the SD card
+		 * controller (SDC2), with a pull-up. The Yoga Slim 7x has no
+		 * card reader which might explain why it has been bridged with another
+		 * pin.
 		 */
-		lid-pull-n-pins {
+		sd-cd-n-pins {
 			pins = "gpio71";
 			function = "gpio";
 			bias-pull-up;
